[vset VERSION 0.1]
[manpage_begin map::track::display n [vset VERSION]]
[category {Map Display and Supporting Utilities}][keywords map]
[keywords {track display, tabular}]
[keywords {tabular, track display}]
[moddesc   {Map display support}]
[titledesc {Widget to display a single track definition}]
[require Tcl 8.6-]
[require Tk  8.6-]
[require debug]
[require debug::caller]
[require map::slippy 0.8]
[require scrollutil]
[require snit]
[require tablelist]
[require map::track::display [opt [vset VERSION]]]
[description]

This package provides a widget to show the information of a single [term geo/track] definition.

[para] The widget shows the statistics of the track, i.e. its center, number of parts, length and
diameter, above a table of its points. Each row of the table shows the number of the point
(counting from 1), its latitude and longitude, the distance from the previous point, and the total
distance along the track so far.

[para] The number of parts is the number of segments of the track, i.e. one less than the number
of its points.

[para] Distances are formatted for display with [cmd {map slippy pretty-distance}] of package
[package map::slippy].

[section API]

[list_begin definitions]
[call [cmd ::map::track::display] [arg pathName] [opt [arg options]...]]

Creates a new track display widget [arg pathName], configured with the specified options. The
result of the command is [arg pathName]. The command is also available as
[cmd {map track display}].

[para] The widget initially shows nothing. Use method [method set] to show a track.

[para] The widget supports the following option:

[list_begin options]
[opt_def -on-selection [arg cmdprefix]]

A command prefix which is invoked when the user selects a row of the table. It is invoked at idle
time, at the global level, with one additional argument, the index of the point shown in the
selected row, counting from 0. The result of the command is ignored.

[para] Selections made through method [method focus] are not reported.

[para] The default is the empty string, i.e. selections are not reported.

[list_end]
[list_end]

The widget supports the standard methods [method cget] and [method configure], and the
following methods:

[list_begin definitions]
[call [arg pathName] [method set] [arg geos]]

Shows the track specified by [arg geos], a list of geo locations, i.e. latitude/longitude pairs,
the points of the track in order. This is the [const geo] element of a [term geo/track] value as
described in [package map::track::file]. An empty list clears the display.

[para] The result of the method is the empty string.

[call [arg pathName] [method focus] [arg index]]

Selects the row of the point with the specified [arg index] in the table, counting from 0, and
scrolls the table to make it visible.

[para] The result of the method is the empty string.

[list_end]

[section EXAMPLE]

[example {
package require map::track::display

map track display .track -on-selection {apply {{index} {
    puts "selected point $index"
}}}
pack .track -fill both -expand 1

.track set {{48.0 11.0} {48.1 11.0} {48.1 11.2}}
}]

